-- title:
--   Transport of Bruhat–Tits tree and PGL₂-action under base change
-- statement:
--   Let $R'$ and $R$ be discrete valuation rings (commutative domains) with fields of fractions $K'$ and $K$ respectively, and let $\iota$ be an integral homomorphism of pairs from $(R',K')$ to $(R,K)$, that is, a ring homomorphism $\iota_{K} : K' \to K$ together with a ring homomorphism $R' \to R$ compatible with the structural maps $R' \to K'$, $R \to K$, and let $\iota'$ be such a homomorphism in the opposite direction, the two field components being mutually inverse ($\iota.\mathrm{toField}\circ\iota'.\mathrm{toField} = \mathrm{id}_K$ and $\iota'.\mathrm{toField}\circ\iota.\mathrm{toField} = \mathrm{id}_{K'}$). Then there exist an isomorphism $e$ of simple graphs between the Bruhat–Tits trees of $(R',K')$ and $(R,K)$ — the vertices being homothety classes of full $R$-lattices in $K^2$, with adjacency generated by the relation `AdjacentLattice` on representatives — and a group isomorphism $\psi : \mathrm{PGL}(2,K') \to \mathrm{PGL}(2,K)$ such that: $e$ agrees pointwise with the base-change map sending the class of a lattice $L'$ to the class of the $R$-span of the image of $L'$ under coordinatewise $\iota_K$; $\psi$ sends the class of $g \in \mathrm{GL}_2(K')$ to the class of the entrywise image $\iota.\mathrm{mapGL}\,g$; $e(g \cdot v) = \psi(g)\cdot e(v)$ for all $g \in \mathrm{PGL}(2,K')$ and all vertices $v$; $e$ carries the standard vertex (the class of the lattice of vectors with integral coordinates) to the standard vertex; and for every group $G$ and every homomorphism $\rho : G \to \mathrm{PGL}(2,K')$, the set of $\gamma \in G$ for which $\psi(\rho(\gamma))$ fixes the standard vertex of $(R,K)$ coincides with the set of $\gamma$ for which $\rho(\gamma)$ fixes the standard vertex of $(R',K')$, and $\psi \circ \rho$ is injective if and only if $\rho$ is.
--
--   This is the transport-of-structure statement accompanying the base-change isomorphism of Bruhat–Tits trees: an isomorphism of pairs (discrete valuation ring, fraction field) induces compatible isomorphisms of the trees and of the acting groups $\mathrm{PGL}_2$, under which the stabiliser of the standard vertex and the injectivity of a presenting homomorphism are preserved. It is used where finiteness of vertex stabilisers and discreteness hypotheses for subgroups of $\mathrm{PGL}_2$ over a local field must be moved between two models of the same pair.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_CerednikDrinfeld_BruhatTits_exists_iso_tree_mulEquiv_projGenLinGroup_baseChange.lean

